# Google Chrome is the desktop's web browser, on purpose.
#
# The base image names no default browser, and Claude Desktop's sign-in hands the
# claude.ai OAuth URL to whatever xdg-open picks. Chrome is the browser this image
# installs and wraps to run here (/usr/local/bin/google-chrome probes for user
# namespaces and uses the basic password store).
#
# Placed in /etc/xdg so GIO and xdg-open both read it; a user's own
# ~/.config/mimeapps.list still outranks it. x-scheme-handler/claude is
# deliberately absent: the claude-desktop package is the only handler for its own
# scheme.
[Default Applications]
x-scheme-handler/http=google-chrome.desktop
x-scheme-handler/https=google-chrome.desktop
text/html=google-chrome.desktop
